## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical considerations for testing a real-time fraud pipeline under backpressure, ensuring end-to-end latency remains bounded while monitoring cascading effects across feature store, cache, and inference.

## Key Concepts

- Backpressure and saturation in microservices
- Tail latency and queue depth as bottleneck signals
- Circuit breakers and graceful degradation
- Observability: tracing, metrics, and dashboards
- Workload modeling with bursts and soak phases

## Code Example

```javascript
